---
/**
 * @file pages/terms.astro
 * @description Terms of use for akibh.dev AND blog.akibh.dev (plan31).
 *
 * WHY THIS CONTENT (POC): only the terms a personal portfolio + blog needs —
 * there is nothing to buy, no accounts and no user uploads except GitHub
 * comments, so no payment/refund/account clauses. Owner decisions:
 *   - blog TEXT © Md Akib Hasan (quote with a link is fine),
 *   - CODE SNIPPETS in posts under the MIT license,
 *   - posts may carry an AI-assistance label (the blog's `ai` frontmatter /
 *     AiBanner), so the no-warranty clause mentions it.
 * The site's own source code is NOT licensed here (the repo is private).
 */
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { portfolioData } from "../data/portfolio";

const { meta } = portfolioData;
const updated = "2026-10-23";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The ground rules for akibh.dev and blog.akibh.dev: reusing posts and code, comments, the contact form, and no warranty."
  updated={updated}
>
  <p class="summary">
    <strong>Short version:</strong> read freely and quote with a link; copy the code snippets into your own projects
    under the MIT license; be decent in the comments; and treat everything here as notes, not guarantees.
  </p>

  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover <a href="https://akibh.dev">akibh.dev</a> and <a href={meta.blogUrl}>blog.akibh.dev</a>, run by
    me, {meta.name}. By using either site you agree to them. How I handle data is in the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Reusing what you find here</h2>
  <h3>Writing</h3>
  <p>
    The text of blog posts and of this portfolio is © {meta.name}. You're welcome to quote short parts with a link
    back to the original. Please don't republish whole posts or large parts of them without asking me first.
  </p>
  <h3>Code snippets</h3>
  <p>
    Code shown in blog posts is licensed under the{" "}
    <a href="https://opensource.org/license/mit">MIT license</a>: use, change and ship it, including commercially. A
    credit is appreciated but not required. Snippets quoted from other projects keep those projects' licenses.
  </p>
  <h3>Names, logos and projects</h3>
  <p>
    Company, product and platform names and logos shown here (GitHub, Cloudflare, LeetCode and others) belong to
    their owners and are used only to identify them. Each project listed on the portfolio has its own license in its
    repository.
  </p>

  <h2>Comments</h2>
  <p>
    Blog comments are GitHub Discussions, so <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service">GitHub's terms</a>{" "}
    apply too. You're responsible for what you post. Keep it on topic and respectful: no spam, ads, harassment, hate,
    illegal content, malware, or other people's private information. I may hide, edit (for example to remove
    personal data) or delete any comment, and block accounts that repeatedly break these rules.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    Use it to reach me — not for spam, automated messages or anything illegal. Please don't send passwords or other
    secrets. I read every genuine message, but I can't promise to answer all of them.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Posts are my own notes and opinions, written as carefully as I can, not professional advice — and not my
    employer's views. Software, commands and services change, so something here may be outdated or wrong. Some posts
    are written with AI assistance; those are labelled at the top. <strong>Check before you rely on anything, and run
    commands and code at your own risk</strong> — test them somewhere safe first. Both sites are provided "as is",
    without warranties, and may change or go offline at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    As far as the law allows, I'm not liable for any loss or damage from using these sites, their content or their
    code, or from sites they link to. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have that the law doesn't allow to be
    limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to other sites are for convenience. I don't control those sites and I'm not responsible for their content
    or policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    I may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version, at{" "}
    <a href="/terms/">akibh.dev/terms/</a>. Questions, corrections or takedown requests:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${meta.email}`}>{meta.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
